1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
In a quiet, sun-scorched village in Bihar, India, a young girl named Mira grew up in poverty.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Her parents were farm laborers who worked tirelessly to provide the basics.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:19,000
By eight, Mira was helping in the fields, carrying bundles, feeding livestock, and often missing school to support her family.

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Yet, deep inside, Mira held a bold dream.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:25,000
She wanted to become a businesswoman.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,000
School was five kilometers away.

7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,000
She walked at barefoot, rain or shine.

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:36,000
With no electricity, she studied by kerosene lamp and borrowed old textbooks.

9
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000
She taught herself English by reading scraps of newspapers and listening to the radio.

10
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,000
What set Mira apart was her determination.

11
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,000
She paid attention to stories of people who rose from poverty, studied their choices, and believed,

12
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,000
one day, I'll stand on my own.

13
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:59,000
At 15, she applied for a national scholarship offered by a non-profit.

14
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Her essay, About Building Businesses That Empower Rural Women, was chosen.

15
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,000
That scholarship changed her life.

16
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Mira moved to Delhi for high school, then earned a full ride to study business in the United States.

17
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:14,000
It wasn't easy.

18
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:18,000
She faced language barriers, culture shock, and homesickness.

19
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,000
But she pressed on.

20
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Years later, she founded a social enterprise in New York,

21
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,000
connecting rural Indian women to global markets.

22
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,000
Her dream wasn't just to succeed.

23
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:32,000
It was to uplift others like her.

24
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Mira's journey wasn't about luck or talent alone.

25
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:40,000
It was about resilience, daily effort, and the courage to grow a little stronger,

26
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:42,000
one percent better, every single day.

